[h1]Random New World (RNW) Generator[/h1]

Procedural New World generator for EU5, inspired by EU4's Conquest of Paradise RNW system — except built from scratch to generate full-scale landmasses rather than stitched-together tiles.

Replaces the Americas with a completely new procedural landmass while keeping the Old World vanilla. Each generated world is exported as a standalone local mod with a short shareable [b]World Code[/b] (seed), so friends on the same game version can generate the exact same map for multiplayer.

[quote][b]⚠️ IMPORTANT: Do not enable THIS workshop item in your playset.[/b]
This workshop item only downloads the external generator tool. The worlds you generate will appear in your mod list as separate local mods (e.g., [i]"RNW: Small continents 7K3Q"[/i]) — enable one of those instead.[/quote]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]5 Landmass Archetypes:[/b] Supercontinent, Continents, Small Continents, Archipelago, or Scattered Islands.
[*][b]Coherent Map Generation:[/b] Elevation, climate zones, river basins, terrain, and vegetation (forests, deserts, jungles) are simulated together rather than placed randomly.
[*][b]Maritime & Naval Layout:[/b] Procedurally named gulfs, straits, and capes, natural harbor placement on coastlines, and seamless integration with vanilla ocean currents and sea lanes.
[*][b]Procedural Natives:[/b] Populated with native tags, cultures, religions, decentralized tribes, settled states, and subject/vassal networks.
[*][b]High American / Fantasy Scenarios:[/b] Optional chance to spawn advanced setups ("Extraordinary peoples") — sprawling empires, maritime merchant leagues, highland confederations, shattered realms, or religious centers.
[*][b]Dynamic Content:[/b] Procedural formable nations, regional colonial naming, and world-specific flavor.
[*][b]True Terra Incognita (Spoiler-Free):[/b] The New World remains hidden on the lobby map and in the mod thumbnail by default, so you won't spoil the geography before sending explorers.
[/list]

[h2]How to Use[/h2]
[olist]
[*]In the EU5 [b]Mods[/b] menu, find [i]Random New World[/i], click [b]Open in folder[/b], and run [b]Random New World Generator[/b].
[*]Select a world archetype, use a random seed, or paste a friend's [b]World Code[/b].
[*]Click [b]Generate[/b]. Generation takes ~2–3 minutes.
[*]Enable the newly created world mod in your playset (only enable one RNW mod at a time) and start a new campaign. The tool will notify you if a game restart is required.
[/olist]

[h2]Customization & Tools[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Quick Presets:[/b] Convenient dropdowns for landmass size, native density, advanced empire ("Extraordinary peoples") spawn chance, and precious metal (gold/silver) abundance.
[*][b]Advanced Sliders:[/b] Fine-tune individual generation parameters under [b]Customize[/b] (clamped to keep every combination playable).
[*][b]Shape Preview & Rerolls:[/b] Use [b]Choose a continent...[/b] to preview 6 coastline sketches before committing. Satisfied with the geography? Use [b]New peoples[/b] or [b]New resources[/b] to reroll political setups or trade goods without changing the terrain.
[*][b]World Atlas:[/b] Built-in viewer to inspect political, culture, religion, resource, and development mapmodes outside the game.
[/list]

[h2]Why an External Generator?[/h2]
EU5's scripting engine cannot dynamically generate heightmaps, terrain meshes, or river topologies at runtime. This tool reads your vanilla EU5 installation files and compiles a standard static map mod.
[list]
[*]Does not modify vanilla game files.
[*]Does not require the game to be open — runs completely standalone.
[*]Requires no internet connection or admin privileges.
[*]The Workshop binary is not the only way to run it: standalone packages and alternative launch options are available on GitHub.
[*]100% open-source (MPL-2.0) with SHA-256 checksums and VirusTotal scans on every GitHub release.
[/list]

[h2]Known Limitations & Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]New saves only:[/b] Not save-game compatible with existing campaigns.
[*][b]Restart between different RNW maps:[/b] Starting a campaign on one RNW map, exiting to menu, and loading a different RNW map in the same session will crash EU5. Restart the game when switching worlds.
[*][b]Game updates:[/b] Major EU5 patches may require a generator update. To continue an old save after a patch, regenerate its world using the same World Code.
[*][b]RAM usage:[/b] Requires ~7.5 GB of free RAM during map compilation. On systems with limited memory, you can close EU5 and run the generator directly from the mod folder to free up RAM (the generator does not require the game to be running).
[/list]

[h2]FAQ[/h2]
[b]Q: Can I preview the map or play as a New World native?[/b]
A: Yes. By default, New World tags are hidden/unselectable in the lobby to prevent spoilers. Click [b]Reveal this world[/b] in the generator (or toggle [b]Show the New World before you play it[/b]) to unmask the lobby map and play as a native tag. [i][TODO: Confirm in release build][/i]

[b]Q: Is it compatible with other mods?[/b]
A: Incompatible with overhaul mods, other map mods, or anything modifying provinces/history in the Americas. UI and Old World flavor mods should work, though compatibility is currently untested.

[b]Q: Does Multiplayer work?[/b]
A: Yes, in theory — every player generates the exact same mod locally using the shared [b]World Code[/b] on the same EU5 patch, resulting in an identical checksum. [i][TODO: Confirm after MP testing][/i]

[b]Q: Ironman & Achievements?[/b]
A: Changes the checksum. [i][TODO: Confirm EU5 achievement rules with modded checksums][/i]

[b]Q: What happens if I unsubscribe from the generator?[/b]
A: Your generated worlds are standalone local mods and will continue to work even if you unsubscribe from this Workshop item. To cleanly uninstall, click [b]Delete world[/b] inside the generator first, then unsubscribe.

[b]Q: Windows SmartScreen / Antivirus warnings?[/b]
A: Every release includes a VirusTotal scan link on GitHub. [i][TODO: Leave either the unsigned Smart App Control note OR the signed certificate note here before publishing][/i]

[b]Q: Does it work on Linux / Steam Deck?[/b]
A: Yes. Clicking [b]Open in folder[/b] from the game menu launches Wine's file explorer inside EU5's Proton prefix, so the generator runs out of the box with zero extra setup. [i][TODO: Confirm on Steam Deck][/i]

[b]Q: How do I report a bug?[/b]
A: In the generator's [b]Settings[/b], click [b]Save diagnostics[/b] (strips out personal usernames/paths) and open a GitHub issue with the log file and your World Code.

